    {
      "id": "claim_2af07d5c3d1f4fef996cf362b672bac5",
      "statement": "generateHarness (src/runner/harness.ts) emits KataRunner.java per run from a kata's Check[], and its design relies on Java overload resolution: toJson(...) has one overload per primitive and array type, so javac picks the right one for whatever the checked method statically returns, meaning the TS codegen never needs to know the target return type — it only renders JavaValue arguments as Java literals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/runner/harness.ts#L1-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c84d375d6b004fa58ac11ea0ba3ec60c8e2f92acec44b5078b958ab9ceaae184:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/runner/harness.ts#L186-L201",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dcb083dc882fc202d98c10aff8e3bc411af699c9909f4caa7e50fc1f70e194ef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_84c331edcbc44805b84574ae1f85a901",
      "statement": "generateHarness emits one check body line per check/case in source order: Main.main(new String[0]) for a stdout check, and rets.add(toJson(Main.<method>(<args>))) per return-check case. This in-order emission is what makes the positional RunResult.returns mapping work in verify.ts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/runner/harness.ts#L128-L139",
