    {
      "id": "claim_1444a52dd52944fd82839b4c7415d133",
      "statement": "KataRunner.main redirects System.out to a ByteArrayOutputStream during the check body, restores it in a finally, then writes results to the real stream using four sentinels: OUT_BEGIN/OUT_END wrap the captured stdout block, RET_PREFIX prefixes each per-case return JSON line (one per return-check case in order), and ERR_PREFIX prefixes a single line carrying t.toString() + the first stack-trace element of a caught Throwable. A thrown exception during any check suppresses all subsequent checks.",
      "evidence": [
