    {
      "id": "claim_5e0f9588b98942499be97f5a3c67ebe3",
      "statement": "compareJavaValue unwraps the {type,value} wrapper on the expected side (unwrapExpected) and dispatches per kind: long is compared as a string (unwrapping an isLongTagged actual.value or String(actual)) to avoid 2^53 precision loss; float/double use EPS=1e-9 with finite check; char compares by codepoint; int by Number equality; plain bare numbers compare by Number (non-integer bare numbers use EPS) and strings/booleans by ===. Arrays compare element-wise with length check first.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/check/verify.ts#L36-L79",
