    {
      "id": "claim_33ab2d7a8f8d4012910d46d5df055730",
      "statement": "JavaValue (src/kata/types.ts) is a discriminated union of bare number/boolean/string/null/array plus an object {type:'long'|'float'|'char'|'double'|'int', value:number|string} type wrapper. The wrapper carries precise primitive kind for values that lose information in JSON/JS (long beyond 2^53 carried as string, float vs double precision, char vs string/number). The harness's toJson overloads emit the same {type,value} shape for long, so expected (kata YAML) and actual (parsed runner JSON) compare with identical unwrap logic.",
